ove has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-9-3{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-9-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+\\frac{b}{c}=-9+\\frac{(-3)}{1}=-12.\n$$" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412659 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412656 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412659 1069 "q-137886" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412659 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412659 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 20 \\\\ 20 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412659 1072 #uuid "8d91806b-81b0-566e-90e0-48dc8925cff9" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412659 1074 "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+40+6=56.\n$$" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412660 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412662 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412660 1062 #uuid "41c0539c-002c-5259-832d-9bb45ac8b928" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412660 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162350 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412661 1062 #uuid "4cdf2d74-0bb9-5a46-a586-06014aa796e7" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412661 1063 #edb/ref 17592186412658 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412662 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412664 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412662 1062 #uuid "887b3834-be22-5f6c-8700-a163d7c04bba" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412662 1063 #edb/ref 17592186412659 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412663 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412660 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412663 1062 #uuid "9b0b78c1-38dc-5b63-a705-26a38e682db9" 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412663 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162349 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412664 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412661 13194139534157 17592186045417 true] [17592186412664 1062 #uuid "bf465